{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792100715,"nonce":"tnyVflgXsOXZkcSuSta3u4GCx6k=","title":"AOT heap allocation embeds compiler-process libc addresses","message":"A native AOT executable built on Linux segfaults before main in __vtable_init__. GDB shows movabs of the compiler process malloc address followed by an indirect call. LLVMJitBackend::build_heap_malloc and build_heap_free emit absolute host addresses for both JIT and AOT; Linux ASLR makes those addresses invalid in the executable. Mac shared-cache addresses masked the failure.\n\nReproducer: haxe-conformance/check-aot-manifest.py, or AOT compile the aot_manifest_entry regression project and run the output on Linux. The manifest bug is separate: class paths now resolve, exposing this allocation fault.\n\nAOT must call relocatable malloc/free symbols, preserving the host-address workaround only for JIT. Add a unit test verifying both symbol calls and run the native executable on Linux and Mac.","files":null}]}